# Normalise line endings.
#
# The t/ scripts are also runnable from bash (Git Bash / WSL / macOS / Linux),
# and bash chokes on CRLF ("$'\r': command not found"). Forcing LF in the
# working tree - even on Windows - keeps them runnable everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is only reliable with CRLF batch files.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pem binary
